<h2 id=3D"2">OSEC-2026-30: OCaml runtime "ephemeron data is freed while sti=
ll referenced"</h2>
<div class=3D"outline-text-2" id=3D"text-2">
</div>
<div id=3D"outline-container-orgff9dccb" class=3D"outline-3">
<h3 id=3D"orgff9dccb">Hannes Mehnert announced</h3>
<div class=3D"outline-text-3" id=3D"text-orgff9dccb">
<p>
Dear everyone,
</p>

<p>
a new advisory was published for the OCaml runtime. Below is the=20
advisory, you can as well find it at=20
<a href=3D"https://github.com/ocaml/security-advisories">https://github.com=
/ocaml/security-advisories</a> and=20
<a href=3D"https://osv.dev/list?q=3D&amp;ecosystem=3Dopam">https://osv.dev/=
list?q=3D&amp;ecosystem=3Dopam</a>
</p>

<p>
In OCaml 5, this is already fixed.
</p>

<p>
Best,
</p>

<p>
Hannes
</p>

<pre class=3D"example" id=3D"orga4e231b">
