<p>
<b>Ephemeron data is freed while still referenced when the key is an=20
<code>Infix_tag</code> closure</b>
</p>
</div>
<div id=3D"outline-container-org724047d" class=3D"outline-4">
<h4 id=3D"org724047d">Summary</h4>
<div class=3D"outline-text-4" id=3D"text-org724047d">
<p>
In OCaml before 4.14.5, when the key of an ephemeron is a closure with=20
<code>Infix_tag</code> (a function of a mutually recursive group that is no=
t the=20
first function), the mark phase does not keep the ephemeron's data=20
alive, although the key is alive. The clean phase does treat the key as=20
alive, so it leaves the data field filled. The sweep phase then frees=20
the data block. After a major collection the ephemeron's data field=20
still points to the freed block.
</p>

<p>
This looks like the part of=20
<a href=3D"https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/7810">#7810</a> that PR=20
<a href=3D"https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/pull/9742">#9742</a> did not cove=
r. PR=20
<a href=3D"https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/pull/9742">#9742</a> fixed the cl=
ean phase=20
and the minor collector. It did not change <code>mark_ephe_aux</code>.
</p>

<p>
Please note that the CVSS score high is under the conditions:
</p>
<ul class=3D"org-ul">
<li><i>if</i> the application is using ephemerons,</li>
<li>and <i>if</i> the application is available over the network,</li>
<li>and <i>if</i> the attacker can find a way to exploit the memory safety<=
/li>
</ul>
<p>
issue in an attack chain.
</p>
</div>
</div>
