</pre>

<p>
<b>Unauthenticated arbitrary file read via path traversal in=20
<code>/conferences/ocaml/**</code></b>
</p>

<p>
<code>GET /conferences/ocaml/&lt;path&gt;</code> on ocaml.org concatenates =
the raw=20
request target onto <code>OCAMLORG_V2_PATH</code> (<code>/v2</code>) and se=
rves it with=20
<code>Dream.from_filesystem</code>, bypassing the path validation that=20
<code>Dream.static</code> performs. An unauthenticated request containing <=
code>..</code>=20
segments escapes <code>/v2</code> and reads arbitrary files as the server p=
rocess,=20
which runs as <code>root</code> in the container.
</p>

<p>
Please note that the live deployment of <a href=3D"https://ocaml.org">https=
://ocaml.org</a> is in a=20
dedicated Docker container which does not contain any secrets. Thus the=20
vulnerability is in the ocaml.org source code, but there has been no=20
impact for the live deployment.
</p>
</div>
