<div id=3D"outline-container-5" class=3D"outline-2">
<h2 id=3D"5">rocq-typescript-extraction (experimental): Extract Rocq defini=
tions to TypeScript ES modules</h2>
<div class=3D"outline-text-2" id=3D"text-5">
<p>
Archive: <a href=3D"https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-rocq-typescript-extract=
ion-experimental-extract-rocq-definitions-to-typescript-es-modules/18734/1"=
>https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-rocq-typescript-extraction-experimental-ex=
tract-rocq-definitions-to-typescript-es-modules/18734/1</a>
</p>
</div>
<div id=3D"outline-container-org884f600" class=3D"outline-3">
<h3 id=3D"org884f600">Sora Morimoto announced</h3>
<div class=3D"outline-text-3" id=3D"text-org884f600">
<p>
I am excited to share an experimental preview of <b>rocq-typescript-extract=
ion</b>, a Rocq plugin that extracts Rocq definitions to TypeScript ES modu=
les.
</p>
</div>
<div id=3D"outline-container-orgd722879" class=3D"outline-4">
<h4 id=3D"orgd722879">What is it?</h4>
<div class=3D"outline-text-4" id=3D"text-orgd722879">
<p>
Rocq (formerly Coq) has long supported extraction to OCaml, Haskell, and Sc=
heme. This plugin adds a TypeScript backend, generating clean ES modules th=
at can be imported and used directly from TypeScript/JavaScript code.
</p>

<p>
The generated code uses erasable TypeScript syntax (no <code>namespace</cod=
e>, <code>enum</code>, <code>declare</code>, or type assertions other than =
<code>as const</code>) and is checked under strict TypeScript settings (<co=
de>--strict --isolatedModules --verbatimModuleSyntax --erasableSyntaxOnly</=
code>). It is intended to run under Bun or Node with type stripping.
</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id=3D"outline-container-org92e85ba" class=3D"outline-4">
<h4 id=3D"org92e85ba">Key capabilities</h4>
<div class=3D"outline-text-4" id=3D"text-org92e85ba">
<ul class=3D"org-ul">
<li>Inductive types (as discriminated unions with a <code>tag</code> proper=
ty), records (as interfaces with <code>readonly</code> properties), recursi=
ve functions, modules, and functors</li>
<li>Number and BigInt presets that map standard integers (<code>nat</code>,=
 <code>positive</code>, <code>N</code>, <code>Z</code>) to JavaScript <code=
>number</code> or <code>bigint</code></li>
<li>Recursive functions (including many mutually recursive ones) become loo=
ps with explicit stacks to avoid JavaScript call-stack limits on deep input=
s</li>
<li>Custom extraction directives (<code>Extract Inductive</code>, <code>Ext=
ract Constant</code>, etc.) for mapping to existing TypeScript types or imp=
lementations</li>
<li>Separate extraction (one file per library with relative imports) or sin=
gle-file extraction</li>
</ul>

<p>
The extraction is designed with performance in mind. The repository include=
s benchmarks (under <code>bench/</code>) that compare extracted code agains=
t handwritten JavaScript/TypeScript implementations across a range of workl=
oads (sorting, persistent data structures, arithmetic, cryptography primiti=
ves from fiat-crypto, and more). The goal is that the extracted code should=
 not have significant performance issues relative to carefully written hand=
written equivalents, particularly when using the Number preset for values t=
hat fit in JavaScript=E2=80=99s safe integer range.
</p>
</div>
<ul class=3D"org-ul">
<li><a id=3D"org36e53ff"></a>Minimal example<br />
<div class=3D"outline-text-5" id=3D"text-org36e53ff">
<p>
Save this as <code>Tree.v</code>:
</p>

<div class=3D"org-src-container">
<pre class=3D"src src-coq"><code><span style=3D"color: #006f00; font-weight=
: bold;">From</span> TypeScriptExtraction <span style=3D"color: #006f00; fo=
nt-weight: bold;">Require Import</span> Number.

<span style=3D"color: #006f00; font-weight: bold;">Inductive</span> <span s=
tyle=3D"color: #a7601f;">tree</span> (<span style=3D"color: #007a9f;">A</sp=
an> : <span style=3D"color: #444fcf; font-weight: bold;">Type</span>) :=3D =
Leaf | Node (<span style=3D"color: #007a9f;">l</span> : tree A) (<span styl=
e=3D"color: #007a9f;">x</span> : A) (<span style=3D"color: #007a9f;">r</spa=
n> : tree A).
<span style=3D"color: #006f00; font-weight: bold;">Arguments</span> Leaf {A=
}.
<span style=3D"color: #006f00; font-weight: bold;">Arguments</span> Node {A=
}.

<span style=3D"color: #006f00; font-weight: bold;">Fixpoint</span> <span st=
yle=3D"color: #a7601f;">size</span> {A} (<span style=3D"color: #007a9f;">t<=
/span> : tree A) : nat :=3D
  <span style=3D"color: #444fcf; font-weight: bold;">match</span> t <span s=
tyle=3D"color: #444fcf; font-weight: bold;">with</span> Leaf =3D&gt; 0 | No=
de l _ r =3D&gt; S (size l + size r) <span style=3D"color: #444fcf; font-we=
ight: bold;">end</span>.

TypeScript <span style=3D"color: #006f00; font-weight: bold;">Extraction</s=
pan> <span style=3D"color: #ca3400;">"tree.ts"</span> size.
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>
Compile it:
