<h2 id=3D"9">Release of Alcotest 1.10 and dune-release 2.3</h2>
<div class=3D"outline-text-2" id=3D"text-9">
<p>
Archive: <a href=3D"https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-release-of-alcotest-1-1=
0-and-dune-release-2-3/18763/1">https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-release-of-=
alcotest-1-10-and-dune-release-2-3/18763/1</a>
</p>
</div>
<div id=3D"outline-container-orgf4cfae0" class=3D"outline-3">
<h3 id=3D"orgf4cfae0">Thomas Gazagnaire announced</h3>
<div class=3D"outline-text-3" id=3D"text-orgf4cfae0">
<p>
Hi everyone,
</p>

<p>
I'm happy to announce the (about to be) release of <code>alcotest 1.10.0</c=
ode> and <code>dune-release 2.3.0</code>. Those two releases contain years =
of backlog for those two projects, so I'm pretty excited they are finally g=
oing out!
</p>

<p>
You can use them by doing:
</p>

<pre class=3D"example" id=3D"org1f8aea2">
opam install dune-release.2.3.0

# https://github.com/ocaml/opam-repository/pull/31135
opam pin add alcotest.1.10.0 --dev
</pre>

<p>
I am particularly thankful for the <a href=3D"https://github.com/mirage/alc=
otest/releases/tag/1.10.0">24 alcotest contributors</a> and <a href=3D"http=
s://github.com/tarides/dune-release/releases/tag/2.3.0">13 dune-release con=
tributors</a> listed on the respective release pages.
</p>

<p>
Here are a few highlights:
</p>

<ul class=3D"org-ul">
<li><i>dune-release</i> now works on Windows (well&hellip; at least <code>d=
istrib</code> and <code>check</code> now work and are tested in the CI) fin=
ishing the work @emillon started in 2021 and follows <code>.gitattributes</=
code> exclusions when generating release archives (thanks to @jjb)!</li>
<li><i>alcotest</i> finally got a few highly-requested features;
<ul class=3D"org-ul">
<li>a bunch of combinators to write tests: <code>suite</code>, <code>test</=
code> and &hellip; <code>group</code>! Yes <b>nested tests are now possible=
</b> without a breaking API change (from @CraigFe's initial RFC, with API i=
nputs from @yawaramin and @mjambon);</li>
<li>every failing test now prints the file and line of your test (inspired =
by @dbuenzli's <a href=3D"https://erratique.ch/software/b0/doc/B0_testing/i=
ndex.html">B0_testing</a>);</li>
<li>test suites can now carry tags (that can be filtered on the command-lin=
e), extending the pre-existing <code>quick</code> / <code>slow</code> arbit=
rary distinction (also from @CraigFe's RFC, but the final implementation an=
d API is quite different to remain backward compatible) ;</li>
<li>a new opt-in mode to generate JUnit XML files, from unmodified test sui=
tes (just set <code>ALCOTEST_JUNIT=3D1</code> in your CI environment) (insp=
ired by @Khady's <a href=3D"https://github.com/Khady/ocaml-junit">junit_alc=
otest</a> idea) ;</li>
<li>and wasm_of_ocaml support (from @hhugo and @mefyl)</li>
</ul></li>
</ul>

<p>
There are a few breaking changes: Alcotest now requires at least OCaml 4.14=
